WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.116 --> 00:00:19.989
Mr. stared at his watch as he waited for the monsters to calm down.

2
00:00:20.009 --> 00:00:23.872
"We're losing precious time," he said.

3
00:00:24.552 --> 00:00:27.635
When everyone had finally grown quiet again, Mr.

4
00:00:27.675 --> 00:00:29.076
Gwarg grabbed his clipboard.

5
00:00:30.164 --> 00:00:32.866
"Let's review our Field Day rules."

6
00:00:32.886 --> 00:00:36.188
"Ugh." Mog groaned.

7
00:00:36.208 --> 00:00:39.210
"We've heard these rules twenty times already!

8
00:00:39.691 --> 00:00:41.012
Can't we just get started?"

9
00:00:41.032 --> 00:00:43.313
"That's enough, Mog!"

10
00:00:43.674 --> 00:00:44.914
Mr. Freaky snapped.

11
00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:47.096
"The rules are important.

12
00:00:47.556 --> 00:00:50.598
That's how everything stays under control around here."

13
00:00:51.299 --> 00:00:53.740
He took out his handkerchief and blew his noses.

14
00:00:57.703 --> 00:01:01.449
first rule—no magic spells," Mr.

15
00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:02.389
Gwarg announced.

16
00:01:02.409 --> 00:01:07.570
"Aww!" Several witches and wizards started complaining.

17
00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:08.991
"What about hexes?"

18
00:01:09.411 --> 00:01:10.271
somebody asked.

19
00:01:10.291 --> 00:01:11.451
"Can we use those?"

20
00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:13.352
"No!" Mr.

21
00:01:13.432 --> 00:01:14.332
Gwarg snapped.

22
00:01:14.352 --> 00:01:16.813
"No magic whatsoever!"

23
00:01:17.813 --> 00:01:19.413
A vampire raised her hand.

24
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:23.375
"Can I turn into a bat and fly around?"

25
00:01:27.076 --> 00:01:28.516
Mr. Gwarg blinked at her.

26
00:01:29.144 --> 00:01:32.125
"You're not even on a team, Vanessa," he said.

27
00:01:32.145 --> 00:01:37.006
"But if you were on a team, yes, you could do that.

28
00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:40.007
That's not magic—it's an ability."

29
00:01:40.027 --> 00:01:43.668
"So it's okay if I make my feet bigger to run faster?"

30
00:01:44.029 --> 00:01:44.869
Carly asked.

31
00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:50.691
The gym teacher scratched his head.

32
00:01:50.711 --> 00:01:52.191
"I guess so.

33
00:01:52.631 --> 00:01:55.292
But I don't think it would actually improve your speed."

34
00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:59.461
Monsters kept raising their hands to ask more questions.

35
00:02:00.342 --> 00:02:01.602
Finally Mr.

36
00:02:01.662 --> 00:02:05.164
Gwarg lifted his whistle and gave a long, loud blast.

37
00:02:07.365 --> 00:02:10.166
"I don't have time to answer all these questions.

38
00:02:10.886 --> 00:02:13.187
Look, there's really only one rule.

39
00:02:13.707 --> 00:02:16.849
And that's this one—just play fair.

40
00:02:17.829 --> 00:02:22.311
Now Team Orange and Team Black, line up for our first event.

41
00:02:23.031 --> 00:02:26.140
It's the tug-of-war!"

42
00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.081
"Phew," Ben murmured to Pixel.

43
00:02:28.101 --> 00:02:29.361
"That took forever."

44
00:02:31.642 --> 00:02:36.403
The spectators cheered as the two teams took their places in the center of the field.

45
00:02:39.424 --> 00:02:44.485
Ben could see that a long rope had been laid over a shallow pit filled with mud.

46
00:02:45.725 --> 00:02:48.666
The teams lined up on opposite sides of the pit.

47
00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:52.807
Then each player gripped the rope.

48
00:02:54.028 --> 00:02:57.841
Suddenly Ben spotted the sixth member of Team Orange.

49
00:02:57.861 --> 00:02:59.622
"Oh, no!"

50
00:03:00.823 --> 00:03:01.483
he gasped.

51
00:03:02.183 --> 00:03:05.665
Last in line on the opposite side of the rope was Gaby.

52
00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:09.246
And Gaby was strong—really strong!

53
00:03:09.926 --> 00:03:12.868
She must be what Zork meant by his "secret weapon."

54
00:03:13.908 --> 00:03:15.409
Waldo had spotted her too.

55
00:03:15.429 --> 00:03:17.790
"Not good," he muttered.

56
00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.471
"Gaby is even stronger when she's mad."

57
00:03:21.371 --> 00:03:22.132
Ben gulped.

58
00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:25.361
"And is she mad about something right now?"

59
00:03:26.141 --> 00:03:27.101
Waldo nodded.

60
00:03:27.121 --> 00:03:29.562
"She's really mad at me.

61
00:03:30.162 --> 00:03:33.383
She said that I should have made Mog choose her for Team Black."

62
00:03:34.243 --> 00:03:35.523
Ben drew in a breath.

63
00:03:35.543 --> 00:03:40.805
"Well, there's no time to worry about that now," he said.

64
00:03:40.825 --> 00:03:42.205
"We're about to start."

65
00:03:42.225 --> 00:03:44.326
"Okay, guys."

66
00:03:44.786 --> 00:03:48.827
Mog turned around to talk to his team from his spot as first in line.

67
00:03:48.847 --> 00:03:50.427
"Here's the plan.

68
00:03:50.948 --> 00:03:55.410
As soon as the game starts, pull the rope as fast and as hard as you can.

69
00:03:55.951 --> 00:03:58.152
Maybe we can take Team Orange by surprise."

70
00:03:58.172 --> 00:03:59.273
"Got it!"

71
00:03:59.754 --> 00:04:02.236
everybody said, gripping the rope tightly.

72
00:04:03.197 --> 00:04:05.178
Mr. Gwarg lifted his whistle.

73
00:04:05.198 --> 00:04:10.122
"The first team to pull the other team into the mud wins," he announced.

74
00:04:10.142 --> 00:04:12.384
"Is everybody ready?"

75
00:04:13.044 --> 00:04:16.407
Both team captains nodded, and then—tweet!

76
00:04:16.447 --> 00:04:18.209
The whistle blew to start the game.

77
00:04:18.229 --> 00:04:19.590
"Pull, Black!"

78
00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:20.791
Mog shouted.

79
00:04:20.811 --> 00:04:22.112
"Pull hard!"

80
00:04:22.668 --> 00:04:26.089
Ben and the others tugged as fast and as hard as they could.

81
00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:29.991
To Ben's surprise, Mog's plan worked perfectly.

82
00:04:30.551 --> 00:04:35.953
In an instant Zork and his team were flying across the ground, and Zork was teetering on the

83
00:04:36.094 --> 00:04:37.054
edge of the mud pit.

84
00:04:37.074 --> 00:04:39.855
"Pull!" Mog screamed.

85
00:04:39.875 --> 00:04:48.719
"Harder!" "Yes!"

86
00:04:49.179 --> 00:04:49.839
Ben thought.

87
00:04:49.859 --> 00:04:51.540
"Zork's going to fall in!

88
00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:52.869
We're going to win!"

89
00:04:53.829 --> 00:04:57.252
Then, with a loud ka-snap!, the rope broke.

90
00:04:58.032 --> 00:05:01.855
Both teams tumbled backward, landing hard on the ground.

91
00:05:01.875 --> 00:05:03.616
"Time out!"

92
00:05:04.156 --> 00:05:07.279
Mr. Gwarg rushed forward to look at the broken rope.

93
00:05:07.299 --> 00:05:10.080
"What in the world happened?

94
00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:12.642
I buy the best ropes in Monsterville.

95
00:05:13.263 --> 00:05:15.264
I've never seen one break before."

96
00:05:16.245 --> 00:05:17.666
Waldo went to take a look.

97
00:05:17.686 --> 00:05:20.407
"I can fix that, Mr.

98
00:05:21.336 --> 00:05:22.396
Gwarg. I know a good spell."

99
00:05:22.416 --> 00:05:23.597
"Me too!"

100
00:05:23.957 --> 00:05:24.917
Brunhilda called.

101
00:05:24.937 --> 00:05:27.678
"Monsters!" Mr.

102
00:05:27.758 --> 00:05:29.458
Freaky was flapping his arms.

103
00:05:29.478 --> 00:05:30.739
"What did Mr.

104
00:05:30.799 --> 00:05:34.219
Gwarg tell you—no magic during Field Day events!"

105
00:05:34.239 --> 00:05:36.960
"Sorry!" Waldo called.

106
00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.761
"We forgot," Brunhilda added.

107
00:05:40.641 --> 00:05:44.042
Mr. Gwarg ran to an equipment shed to get another rope.

108
00:05:45.282 --> 00:05:47.883
Then he told the two teams to line up again.

109
00:05:47.903 --> 00:05:51.064
"Okay, everyone, take your places."

110
00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:54.983
The teams gathered on their sides of the pit once more.

111
00:05:55.003 --> 00:05:58.145
"Go!" Mr.

112
00:05:58.205 --> 00:06:02.669
Gwarg shouted, and both teams began pulling with all their might again.

113
00:06:03.169 --> 00:06:09.534
This time, though, Team Orange wasn't surprised by Team Black's strategy; they were ready for it.

114
00:06:10.355 --> 00:06:15.679
Back and forth the rope tugged for several minutes, with neither team making much progress.

115
00:06:17.932 --> 00:06:23.902
The spectators on the field were cheering loudly as the cheerleaders did cartwheels across the field.

116
00:06:23.922 --> 00:06:26.126
"Go, Orange!

117
00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:27.648
Go, Black!"

118
00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.895
Then all at once, the air went deadly silent.
